  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Georgia recorded $52.7M in contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Georgia saw 1,206 awards, with an average award size of $43.7K, and obligations were down 99.5% year over year. Prior fiscal years show much larger annual totals: FY22 totaled $8.5B, FY23 totaled $11.1B, FY24 totaled $10.4B, FY25 totaled $11.6B, and FY26 totaled $9.8B. The FY2027 to date total is concentrated in a few buyers and industries: the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $48.8M, and Temporary Help Services accounted for $12.1M of obligations. The FY2027 to date list of top vendors includes FLIGHTWORKS INC and VETMED GROUP LLC at $4.7M each, ARROW ARC LLC at $3.9M, and JMG VETERAN CONTRACTING LLC at $3.8M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). This page summarizes the state-level spending pattern, buying agencies, leading vendors, and the NAICS industries that received the largest shares of FY2027 to date obligations in Georgia.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why are FY2027 obligations so small compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Georgia obligations in FY2027 to date totaled $52.7M, compared with prior full fiscal years that ranged from $8.5B to $11.6B. Obligations are down 99.5% year over year, so FY2027 to date represents a steep drop relative to FY26, which totaled $9.8B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in FY2027 to date with $48.8M, which explains much of the current total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors account for most FY2027 to date obligations?",
        "body": "Temporary Help Services is the largest industry in FY2027 to date with $12.1M in obligations, followed by Ambulance Services with $9.4M and Cut Stone and Stone Product Manufacturing with $6.9M. FLIGHTWORKS INC and VETMED GROUP LLC are the top vendors in FY2027 to date with $4.7M each, and ARROW ARC LLC and JMG VETERAN CONTRACTING LLC follow with $3.9M and $3.8M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Georgia?",
      "a": "Georgia received $52.7M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Georgia had 1,206 awards and the average award size was $43.7K. Obligations were down 99.5% year over year, and prior full fiscal years show totals of $8.5B in FY22, $11.1B in FY23, $10.4B in FY24, $11.6B in FY25, and $9.8B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Georgia?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs awards the most contracts in Georgia, obligating $48.8M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Justice obligated $4.9M, the Department of Transportation obligated $1.5M, and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $1.3M. Other buyers in the top ten include the General Services Administration at $1M and the Department of Agriculture at $170K."
